🧠 OOP Concept Used

Inheritance and Polymorphism

The program uses a virtual "calculateRent()" function in the base class. The "Bike" class overrides this function to apply a different rental calculation.

This demonstrates runtime polymorphism, where different vehicle types can provide their own implementation of the same function.

---

🎯 Objective

To understand how inheritance, virtual functions, and function overriding can be used to implement different rental calculations for different types of vehicles.

